questions.explanation:
The centroid of the shaped portion of the disc is given by, [latex]\; \; \; x=\frac{A_{1}x_{1}+A_{2}x_{2}}{A_{1}+A_{2}}[/latex] where x is the radial distance from O. [latex]\begin{aligned}
  A_{1}&=\, \pi r^{2};\; x_{1}=0;\\  A_{2}&=-\pi \times \left ( \frac{r}{2} \right )^{2}=-\frac{\pi r^{2}}{4}\\  x_{2}&=\frac{r}{2}\\ \therefore \;   x&=\frac{\pi r^{2}\times 0-\frac{\pi r^{2}}{4}\times \frac{r}{2}}{\pi r^{2}-\frac{\pi r^{2}}{4}}\\  x&=\frac{\pi r^{2}\times 0-\frac{\pi r^{2}}{4}\times \frac{r}{2}}{\pi r^{2}-\frac{\pi r^{2}}{4}}\\ \Rightarrow \; x&=-\frac{r}{6}
\end{aligned}[/latex]

